      "description": "Standardize MegaSAM camera trajectories and depth-backprojected per-frame points as three timed colmap4d components.",
      "category": [
        "reconstruction",
        "megasam"
      ],
      "docs": "Standardizes MegaSAM camera trajectories and per-frame point clouds into three scalar colmap4d application components. Points are depth-backprojected XYZ/RGB with source-frame exposure-center nanoseconds and reciprocal COLMAP observations. Binary encoding only. Components must be assembled before validate_full.\n\nRuns the existing Depth-Anything, UniDepth, MegaSAM, RAFT and CVD chain through sharp_repo/per-frame/video_to_colmap.py --convert-only --track_megasam. This use of the tracking wrapper does not run SHARP: Gaussian inference, optimization and completion are outside this pack. Depth NPZ and caches are private scratch, not ports. A private copy of megasam_repo protects native sources from outputs_cvd writes.\n\nDefault exposure_metadata requires a JSON file bound to video_sha256, clock_domain and decoded-index exposure centers. pts_estimate explicitly treats actual video PTS as approximate exposure centers; synthetic_uniform requires positive fps_num/fps_den. Skip/cap preserve original decoded indexes. See README.md and docs/colmap4d-components.md in the source repository. Video input is one file or a handle directory containing exactly one video. SDR inputs only; unsupported HDR/color primaries fail before inference. Rotation metadata is not applied. Scratch retains native products for diagnosis and can exceed 40 GB for long clips.\n\nInput frames accepts video-source OR array[frame]<image>. For videos, timestamp_mode and fps_num/fps_den are unchanged. For image arrays, exposure_metadata_path takes precedence (same exposure-center records, bound by frames_sha256); otherwise use complete HoloLab XMP exposure times, otherwise require explicit frames_fps for synthetic_uniform. Invalid/partial metadata is an error, not a fallback. timestamp_mode/fps_num/fps_den do not select array timing. Frames sort by element filename before skip/cap. See README.md for the deterministic array identity and color rules. Outputs are named 4d_cams, 4d_points, 4d_images; component tags are unchanged.\n",
      "source_entry": "run.py",
